   {
    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     91,
     103
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests for {@link Symmetry454Chronology} and {@link Symmetry454Date}. <p> Background needed to read the test data below: <ul> <li>A Symmetry454 year has 12 months. In each quarter the months follow a 4-5-4 week pattern, so the middle month of every quarter (February, May, August, November) has 35 days while all other months have 28 days.</li> <li>A normal year has 364 days (52 weeks). A leap year appends a \"leap week\" to December, giving it 35 days and the year 371 days.</li> <li>{@code 0001/01/01 (Sym454)} is aligned with {@code 0001-01-01 (ISO)}.</li> </ul>"
   },
